# 6. Dependency Rule

Dependency Injection only.

Forbidden:

```cpp
Singleton::Instance()
Global Objects
Hidden Dependencies
```

Allowed:

```cpp
Process(
EngineContext&
)
```

Every dependency must appear in the function signature.

---

# 7. Engine Context

Reserved objects:

```text
PortfolioContext
        │
        ▼
CSymbolContext
        │
        ▼
Engine Modules
```

One SymbolContext per instrument.

No shared symbol state.

---

# 8. Event System

Event Bus responsibilities:

* Route events
* Queue events
* Publish events
* Maintain short RAM history
* Send persistence queue

Never:

* Make trading decisions
* Run audits

---

# 9. Event Audit

Module 11

Responsible for:

* Event inspection
* Event enrichment
* Trigger audit requests

No infrastructure.

---

# 10. Audit Engine

Responsible for:

* Contract validation
* Registry integrity
* Ownership verification
* Dependency verification

Produces

PASS

WARNING

FAIL

---

# 11. Analytics

Read-only.

Reads SQLite.

Never changes engine state.

Produces:

* Win rate
* RR
* Session reports
* POI reports
* Liquidity reports

---

# 12. Registry Rules

Every registry:

* Immutable
* Versioned
* Single writer
* Append only

Every entry has:

* Base ID
* Instance ID
* Version
* Timestamp
* Integrity
* Status

---

# 13. Registry Manager

Responsible only for:

* Retention
* Snapshot
* Versioning
* Archival

Never writes business data.

Modules own their registries.

---

# 14. Persistence

RAM

↓

Persistence Queue

↓

SQLite

SQLite failure

↓

Persistence Error

↓

Engine continues

Persistence is never a dependency.

---

# 15. Snapshot Strategy

Snapshot:

* Counters
* Registry metadata
* Active recommendations
* Correlation IDs

Market-derived state

↓

Rebuild from replay

Broker state

↓

Restore from snapshot

---

# 16. Recovery Strategy

On startup:

If snapshot exists

↓

Load

↓

Replay missing bars

↓

Continue

If snapshot missing

↓

Replay historical bars

↓

Rebuild engine

↓

Continue

---

# 17. Integrity Rules

Fail closed.

Integrity is scoped.

Scope contains:

* Symbol
* Broker
* Module

Integrity failure affects only its scope.

---

# 18. Versioning

Every contract includes:

```text
SchemaVersion

EngineVersion
```

Every registry entry stores:

* Schema Version
* Engine Version

This guarantees future compatibility.

---

# 19. Testing

